Id":"nightowl-archive","blockId":"clue-keeper","hints":["Someone signing as \"Keeper\" posted on a late-night bulletin board.","Look in the message archive of the Night Owl Bulletin."]},{"clueId":"keeper-lantern","pageId":"bytemarket-classifieds","blockId":"clue-brass","hints":["Somebody is selling something that does not belong in a computer shop.","Read the classified ads at Byte Market."]},{"clueId":"keeper-word","pageId":"chugging-notices","blockId":"clue-notice","hints":["The last word is pinned up where the coffee is.","Read the notice board at Chugging Coffee House."]}],"reward":{"documentId":"keepers-log","vfsPath":"C:\\My Documents\\Keepers Log.txt","title":"The Keeper's Log","text":"THE KEEPER'S LOG - LANTERN POINT LIGHT\r\nLast page, recovered December 1995\r\n\r\nNovember 30, 1971\r\nLast night of the light. Clear sky, calm sea. I lit the lamp\r\nat 4:52 and flashed our old signal one more time:\r\nthree, two, three. It spells W-R-E-N on the family code,\r\nfor my granddaughter, who is three years old and asleep.\r\n\r\nSomeday someone will see it and wonder.\r\nLeave the brass lantern with Dot. Keep the logbook dry.\r\nAnd if anyone asks what a lighthouse is for, tell them:\r\nso that nobody is ever out there alone in the dark.\r\n\r\nNIGHTLIGHT.\r\n\r\n-- H. Holloway, Keeper\r\n\r\n(Found by you, with help from Northstar, the Night Owl,\r\nByte Market and Chugging Coffee House. Thank you. -- Wren)\r\n"}}],"aolKeywords":[{"keyword":"news","target":"aol-area:news"},{"keyword":"mail","target":"aol-area:mail"},{"keyword":"chat","target":"aol-area:chat"},{"keyword":"people","target":"aol-area:chat"},{"keyword":"games","target":"aol-area:games"},{"keyword":"internet","target":"aol-area:internet"},{"keyword":"web","target":"aol-area:internet"},{"keyword":"coffee","target":"http://chugging.test/"},{"keyword":"switchboard","target":"http://switchboard.test/"},{"keyword":"packet","target":"http://packet.test/"},{"keyword":"northstar","target":"http://northstar.t